<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch central bank allocates fresh liquidity.</title>
<headline>Dutch central bank allocates fresh liquidity.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-09-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Dutch central bank said on Wednesday it had allocated 1.66 billion guilders to the money market under a five-day special advances pact at an unchanged rate of 2.50 percent.</p>
<p>Individual banks' applications were met for 5.5 percent.</p>
<p>The pact replaces a five-day facility of 4.15 billion guilders, which expired today.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsdesk +31 20 504 5000 (fax +31 20 5040)</p>
